Hrmp.  Are the foo-proofed items wishes?  I hope they weren't, though
none of those items are worth foo-proofing by hand (unless you used ?
destroy armor, though all other items are more important than the T-
shirt for that)

If the t-shirt was wished, probably not worth it; a marker'd help your
AC more.
I'd ditch the GoPower for leather gloves (you have a good chance of
finding +2 or better in the Castle or Ludios or somewhere), unless
maybe if you're a dwarf.  Human valks in particular should have no
need for GoPower post-quest; as a dwarf I'd still prefer the leather
but it's arguable. Likewise I'd trade the elven cloak for a robe soon.
I'd also think about jumping boots instead of speed boots, but there
are benefits to both, and speed boots are better if you're not going
to remember to jump.  Jumping makes the Sanctum and Astral a _lot_
easier.

For a first-timer, SDSM + CoMagic Resistance would open up
"oLifeSaving, which gives you a buffer against mistakes (particularly
the kind from seeing things you've never seen before).  I prefer your
layout to allow a robe, but that's trading safety for convenience.
